# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_fork_pr_path.py" "FORK-PR PATH GATE: PASS" "fork-PR path" "fork-PR path (base-keyed account+coordinate; a forged-coordinate fork can't cross-tenant write; check degrades to comment-only on the fork-head sha without crashing; missing live fork identity redacts without disabling merge gating; no fork token / no fork API call; content-free)" "fork-PR / external-contributor path (a PR from a FORK keys on the BASE repo, not the fork: base-keyed account+coordinate; a malicious fork forging another tenant's owner-id/full_name can NOT cross-tenant write [moat]; the check degrades to comment-only when the fork-head sha rejects [never crash]; a normal live webhook whose deleted fork has head.repo=null selects privacy redaction while preserving action_required behavior; no token requested for / no API call against the fork; the fork's file BODIES never stored [content-free]; SECURITY-critical)" 20
